From 82184bbc386d887a1196adff53e4ed7d0d69ee00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvamalfa <salvamalfas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:13:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] Settle the seed question and package the PNT request

Measured which seeds actually work, then built everything the chosen one
needs.

Seed findings (backtest against T-100, competitive routes, 2025):
- seats 1.40 pp / 4.21%, flight counts 1.98 pp / 5.96%
- presence only, no frequencies: 13.04 pp / 39.38%
- national market share as seed: 153% error, with 75% of passengers landing
  on routes the carrier does not fly

National share cannot serve as a seed at all: it is mathematically identical
to a seed of ones, because the fit cancels any column scaling. It is already
in the model as the column marginal. Chaining an IPF over AFAC's published
route flight counts adds nothing for the same reason.

So the seed must carry frequencies, which rules out route maps and airport
destination tables. Default provider is a schedules API emitting
period_id, origin_iata, dest_iata, carrier_key, flights.

Adds build_seed_from_flights, which rekeys a provider table into AFAC's city
vocabulary and raises UnmappedSeedError rather than silently dropping an
airport it cannot place. Adds two crosswalks: 52 AFAC cities to IATA, each
verified against dim_airport, and AFAC carrier names to carrier_key.
load_afac_domestic_margins now emits carrier_key so seed and margins share
identities.

Adds docs/solicitud-pnt.md: the request text ready to paste, form field
values, and the articles of the transparency law published 20 March 2025,
which replaced the 2015 law whose numbering older templates still cite.

The email route bounced: 550 5.4.1 from the AFAC tenant is a recipient-level
rejection, not a content one. The copy to the SICT transparency unit was
delivered.

